Geany @VERSION@ - the programmer's editor (GTK 3) for RISC OS

Geany 2.1 by the Geany contributors (GPL version 2), on GTK 3 through
riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend. A demonstration of a large program built
for RISC OS with riscos-gtk's devkit: it isn't changed for RISC OS beyond
where it finds its data.

Using it
- Run it: Geany opens its window and puts its icon on the icon bar. Or
  drop a file on !Geany in a Filer window.
- The icon bar icon: Select brings Geany's window to the front; Menu
  gives Info, Choices... (Geany's Preferences) and Quit.
- Text, HTML, XML, CSS, JavaScript, JSON and CSV files double-clicked in
  the Filer while Geany is loaded, dropped on its icon or window, or saved
  to it from another program, open in a tab of their own.
- Click Menu over the window for Geany's menus, or use its menu bar.
  Keyboard short-cuts are shown in the menus (^S save, ^O open...).
- File > Save As: a RISC OS Save box. Drag its icon to a Filer window, or
  give a full name and click Save. Names without an extension are saved
  as Text (&FFF). File > Open: an Open box; drag a file to it.
  Click Browse... in either box for the directory browser (a Filer-like
  window with a sidebar of discs and places), or *Set RISCOS_GTK_CHOOSER
  filer to have it every time.
- Quit (or a desktop shutdown) with unsaved documents asks: Cancel or
  Discard.
- Geany's settings are kept in <Choices$Write>.geany.
- Build menu: Compile, Build, Make and the rest run in a task window in
  the background, and their messages appear in Geany's Compiler tab
  (click an error to go to its line); Stop ends them. Execute runs the
  program in a task window of its own and shows its return code. The
  commands must be ones RISC OS has: for C, GCC and make (PackMan), or
  change them with Build > Set Build Commands.
- Not in this build: plugins and the built-in terminal (VTE).

Messages
Geany's messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.Geany.Log.

Needs
RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 or later machine (Raspberry Pi 2 or later, ARMX6,
Titanium...), SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv
(PackMan). PThreadTicker is included.

